    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "Assume that for every $ t\\in \\mathbb{N}_{\\geq 1} $, $ f_t $ is convex, $ \\|f_t\\|_{\\infty} \\leq M $ on $ \\constraint $, $ \\sup_{\\Bx\\in \\constraint} \\|\\nabla f_t(\\Bx)\\|\\leq G $, $ r B^n\\subseteq \\constraint \\subseteq RB^n $, and that the diameter of $ \\constraint $ is $ D<\\infty $. If we set $ \\eta = \\frac{D}{\\sqrt{2}nM}T^{-4/5} $, $ \\sigma_t = t^{-2/5} $, $ \\delta = c T^{-1/5} $, and $ \\alpha=\\delta/r < 1$ ... the expected regret ... is at most \\frac{\\sqrt{2}nMD}{c^2}T^{3/5} + (\\sqrt{2}nMD+ \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{4}DG+3cG+cRG/r)T^{4/5}."
   },
